# Project context

## Identity

- Project name: À ta soif ! (atasoif-v2)
- Project type: MOBILE_APPLICATION + API (Angular/Capacitor + AdonisJS)
- Status: DEVELOPMENT
- Repository root: this directory only (`atasoif-v2`). Do **not** place project rules, `package.json`, `pnpm-workspace.yaml`, `node_modules`, or `.pnpm-store` in the parent `atasoif/` folder (legacy projects live there separately).
- Primary language for client-facing content: FR
- Supported locales: FR only (MVP)
- Future i18n: optional evolution via a `locales/` (or equivalent) folder — do not implement until explicitly requested

## Product purpose

Core job-to-be-done: remember what you drank. You buy a bottle (e.g. whisky), and months later you still know where you got it, how much you paid, and whether it was good — notes, review, price, place/supplier, photo.

Digital multi-alcohol cellar (whisky, rum, beer, wine, and more) on top of that memory problem: shared catalog for fast add, personal collection with editable overrides, freemium → subscription. Social and growth features are secondary. Do **not** copy the current atasoif.fr v1 UX as the target; use the memory JTBD as the design north star.

## Scope

### Included

- Shared bottle catalog + personal collection with freemium gate (10 bottles)
- Auth: email/password + Ally social (Google, Apple, **Facebook**)
- Wine and extensible alcohol categories
- Subscriptions: 3.99€/month, 39.99€/year
- Capacitor iOS/Android builds from `apps/web`
- Later: friends, collection sharing, messaging, catalog seed/sync (Open Food Facts)

### Excluded

- In-app AI (recommendations, photo recognition, chat)
- Bright Data / aggressive scrapers as the primary catalog strategy
- Multilingual UI for MVP (FR only; later possible via `locales/`)
- NestJS / Prisma / Better Auth (replaced by Adonis — see `docs/STACK-ADONIS.md`)
- Relying on Facebook Graph “all friends” import (Meta-restricted; use in-app friends + optional FB login)

Do not implement excluded or speculative features without an explicit request.

## Stack

- Backend: **AdonisJS 7** (API) + **Lucid** + **Auth** + **Ally** + PostgreSQL 16
- Frontend: Angular 20 (+ Capacitor later)
- Database: PostgreSQL 16
- Cache or queue: none yet
- Infrastructure: OVH VPS (target); Docker Compose for API + Postgres
- Package manager: pnpm at monorepo root; Adonis app may use its own lockfile under `apps/api`
- Node: **≥ 24** for Adonis 7 (Docker + local via nvm/Herd)

See `docs/STACK-ADONIS.md`.

## Architecture

- Architectural style: modular monolith (monorepo) with Adonis MVC API
- Main modules or bounded contexts:
  - Catalog (`Bottle`, `Category`, `BottleSource`)
  - Collection (`UserBottle` with field/photo overrides)
  - Auth (Adonis Auth + Ally providers)
  - Billing (`Subscription`)
  - Social (friends, messages — post-MVP)
- Dependency direction: `apps/web` → API HTTP; `apps/api` → Lucid → PostgreSQL; shared constants via `@atasoif/shared` when practical
- Important existing abstractions to reuse:
  - `packages/shared` constants (`FREE_BOTTLE_LIMIT`, plans, categories)
  - Design tokens in `apps/web/src/styles/_tokens.scss`

Do not introduce a new architectural pattern without explaining why the existing structure cannot support the requirement.

## Domain rules

- Freemium: max 10 bottles total in collection without an active subscription
- Catalog is global; personal edits use `UserBottle` overrides (do not mutate global `Bottle` by default on user edit)
- Add-bottle UX: search catalog first → prefill → all fields + photo editable → confirm (<30s path)
- Memory fields matter most: price paid, where bought (supplier/place), personal note/review, photo — not social vanity
- Client-facing copy: French, informal “tu”, short and slightly playful
- Design direction: dark cellar / amber (see `docs/DESIGN.md`)
- Do not treat atasoif.fr v1 UI as the target experience

Domain rules take precedence over technical convenience.

## Data and privacy

- Personal data processed: email, name, pseudo, auth tokens, collection data, messages (when enabled), OAuth profile data from Ally providers
- Sensitive data processed: password hashes via Adonis Auth; payment handled by store IAP providers
- Retention requirements: not fully specified — flag before implementing deletion/export flows
- Regulatory constraints: RGPD (privacy policy, deletion rights); App Store age rating 17+; no promotion of excessive drinking

Never infer legal, privacy, or retention requirements that are not documented. Flag missing decisions.

## Authentication and authorization

- Authentication method: Adonis Auth (email/password + access tokens) + Ally (Google, Apple, Facebook)
- Roles and permissions: authenticated user; admin TBD
- Critical authorization rules:
  - Users may only mutate their own `UserBottle`, friendships, and messages
  - Freemium limit enforced server-side
  - Authorization must be enforced server-side even when the UI hides restricted actions

Facebook via Ally is for **login**. In-app friends (E6) remain the source of truth — do not depend on Meta friend-list APIs.

## Frontend and UX

- Design system or component library: custom tokens (cave nocturne); no Material-by-default
- Responsive targets: mobile-first (store apps primary)
- Accessibility target: WCAG 2.2 AA
- Browser or device support: modern iOS/Android WebViews + recent mobile Chrome/Safari; desktop secondary
- Known component-reuse exceptions: none yet

Critical conversion UX documented in `docs/UX-ADD-BOTTLE.md`.  
Delivery plan: `docs/EPICS.md` + `docs/SPRINTS.md` + `docs/tickets/` (orchestrator tickets for sub-agents).  
