## Explicit exceptions to reusable rules

- No dedicated Adonis stack rules in the shared cursor-rules library yet — follow official Adonis/Lucid/Ally docs via Context7.
- Photo storage may start on the VPS filesystem before object storage — Reason: cost on OVH 8€ VPS — Scope: media upload module

## Current constraints and known risks

- Solo developer; ship MVP (cave + freemium + stores) before social/messaging
- Adonis scaffold landed; implement E1 Auth/Ally tickets next (Nest only in `archive/nest-api`)
- Catalog quality drives conversion; seed required before growth
- Acquisition/marketing is the main business risk, not the tech stack
- Apple Sign In required when shipping social login on iOS
- Legacy v1 data (~9 bottles) to migrate from Railway Postgres

## Definition of done

A task is complete only when all applicable conditions are met:

- The requested behavior works and respects domain rules.
- Existing architecture and components were reused where appropriate.
- Relevant tests were added or updated and pass.
- Linting, formatting, type checks, and builds pass when applicable.
- Security and dependency checks pass when applicable.
- Client-facing content uses French; code/docs/commits use English.
- Accessibility and responsive behavior were verified for frontend changes.
- Documentation was updated when commands, architecture, configuration, or behavior changed.
- No secret, debugging artifact, dead code, or unexplained workaround remains.
